        <mxCell id="UnI0fS5W2R1EIqpq5tZH-37" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;h1 class=&quot;c-article-satellite-title u-h1&quot; data-test=&quot;top-caption&quot; id=&quot;Fig7&quot; style=&quot;font-size: min(max(1.5rem, 4vw), 2rem); margin: 0.67em 0px 16px; font-weight: 700; -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; font-family: Harding, Palatino, serif; letter-spacing: min(max(-0.0117156rem, 4vw), -0.0390625rem); line-height: 1.4; box-sizing: inherit; word-break: break-word; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;&quot;&gt;Extended Data Fig. 1&lt;/h1&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="104" width="304" x="65.99662597656251" y="1899.996748046875" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="UnI0fS5W2R1EIqpq5tZH-38" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;h1 class=&quot;c-article-satellite-title u-h1&quot; data-test=&quot;top-caption&quot; id=&quot;Fig7&quot; style=&quot;font-size: min(max(1.5rem, 4vw), 2rem); margin: 0.67em 0px 16px; font-weight: 700; -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; font-family: Harding, Palatino, serif; letter-spacing: min(max(-0.0117156rem, 4vw), -0.0390625rem); line-height: 1.4; box-sizing: inherit; word-break: break-word; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;&quot;&gt;Fig. 1&lt;/h1&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="104" width="95" x="4" y="597" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="UnI0fS5W2R1EIqpq5tZH-39" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;h3 class=&quot;c-article__sub-heading&quot; id=&quot;Sec4&quot; style=&quot;-webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, Roboto, Oxygen-Sans, Ubuntu, Cantarell, &amp;quot;Helvetica Neue&amp;quot;, sans-serif; letter-spacing: -0.0117156rem; font-size: 1.5rem; line-height: 1.24; box-sizing: inherit; font-style: normal; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); margin: 24px 0px 8px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;2. Epigenetic regulation of antigen presentation&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="84" width="635" x="2076" y="412" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="UnI0fS5W2R1EIqpq5tZH-40" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;h3 class=&quot;c-article__sub-heading&quot; id=&quot;Sec3&quot; style=&quot;-webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, Roboto, Oxygen-Sans, Ubuntu, Cantarell, &amp;quot;Helvetica Neue&amp;quot;, sans-serif; letter-spacing: -0.0117156rem; font-size: 1.5rem; line-height: 1.24; box-sizing: inherit; font-style: normal; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); margin: 0px 0px 8px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;1. Multimodal immune analysis of CRC microbiopsies&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="90" width="601" x="15" y="457" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="UnI0fS5W2R1EIqpq5tZH-44" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;Their previous Nature paper show&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;ed t&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot;&gt;hat&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(34, 34, 34); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;somatic chromatin accessibility alterations (&lt;/span&gt;SCAAs)&lt;/b&gt; rewire TF binding → disrupt interferon signaling → Suggest epigenetic suppression of immune response&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;Methods: examined the role of the epigenome in enabling im&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;mune escape by looking for &lt;b&gt;SCAAs &lt;/b&gt;associated with &lt;b&gt;APGs &lt;/b&gt;in 25 CRCs&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Results:&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;45 SCAAs identified in APG promoters (25 CRCs)&lt;br&gt;62% (21/34) APGs affected&lt;br&gt;36% (9/25) patients with ≥1 APG disruption&lt;br&gt;42 (93%) of the SCAAs were losses of accessibility, significantly different than expected based on the genome-wide distribution of SCAAs&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;None of the SCAAs co-occurred with somatic mutations in those genes&lt;/b&gt; (Fig. 2a).&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;This exclusivity could indicate that mutations are more likely to be found in expressed genes or that SCAAs are an alternate route to antigen presentation disruption.&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="491" width="708" x="2067" y="535" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="UnI0fS5W2R1EIqpq5tZH-46" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="Text" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="60" x="3106" y="729" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="UnI0fS5W2R1EIqpq5tZH-49" edge="1" parent="1" source="UnI0fS5W2R1EIqpq5tZH-47" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.836;entryY=0.002;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;entryPerimeter=0;" target="UnI0fS5W2R1EIqpq5tZH-44">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="UnI0fS5W2R1EIqpq5tZH-47" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;SCAAs&lt;br style=&quot;padding: 0px; margin: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;Detection: Compare ATAC-seq (tumor vs normal glands), correct for purity + copy number → Define SCAAs&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;padding: 0px; margin: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;APG-gene: Keep SCAAs in promoter/enhancer regions, linked to antigen-presenting genes (APGs)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;padding: 0px; margin: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;Folder changes: Lossof SCAA: FC &amp;lt; −1; Gain of SCAA: FC &amp;gt; 1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;padding: 0px; margin: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;Significance: 200 random gene sets → expected distribution → Empirical P-value for enrichment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="250" width="477" x="2741" y="218" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FLlcXo33fteFZTflUlvy-1" parent="1" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/png,;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="251.2" width="293.83" x="2812.17" y="1144.8" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FLlcXo33fteFZTflUlvy-2" parent="1" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/png,;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="565.48" width="590" x="2775" y="520" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FLlcXo33fteFZTflUlvy-3" parent="1" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/png,;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="228" width="234.71" x="3150" y="1153.0000000000002" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FLlcXo33fteFZTflUlvy-4" parent="1" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/png,;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="485" width="488.82" x="2872" y="1415" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FLlcXo33fteFZTflUlvy-7" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Which transcription factors (TFs) may drive epigenetic silencing of APGs?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;10 promoter regions (ATAC peaks) repeatedly lose accessibility (&amp;gt;1 patient), affacting 8 APGs. &lt;b&gt;(&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;Extended Data Fig. 3a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;10 TFs that bound &amp;gt; 2 of these regions, most notably NFIC, which had binding sites in the silenced promoter of all eight recurrently SCAA-affected APGs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;TFs had a high number of binding sites genome-wide, they were enriched for APG-SCAA-loss site binding&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Impact of SCAA Loss on APG Expression&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;1. Example: ERAP2, SCAA-loss → lower expression: Affected cancers: 6.8 (VST) vs. Normal tissue: 7.9. Unaffected cancers: 8.1&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;(&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;Extended Data Fig. 3b&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;2. Global pattern: no consistent decrease across all genes/patients → Effect is variable&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;(&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;Extended Data Fig. 3b&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;3. Chromatin ↔ Expression relationship: Promoter accessibility ↑ → gene expression ↑.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;Spearman R = 0.12 (P &amp;lt; 1e−16); stronger in low-expression genes (R = 0.19)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;→ Accessibility is positively associated with expression&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;4. Interpretation: SCAAs are permissive, not deterministic, do not always directly change expression&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;5. They examined heritability of APG expression using phylogenetic signal analysis.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;- Strong or recurrent phylogenetic signal correlated with subclonal HLA LOH and subclonal differences in the pattern of open chromatin in cancer C559&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;- Mostly low phylogenetic signal, expression varies across subclones&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;→&amp;nbsp; Indicates high intratumor heterogeneity&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="855" width="738" x="2067" y="1026" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FLlcXo33fteFZTflUlvy-8" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;b style=&quot;forced-color-adjust: none; caret-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Helvetica; font-size: 12px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(236, 236, 236); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;forced-color-adjust: none; background-color: transparent; font-size: 20px; caret-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;Extended Data Fig. 3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="46" width="249" x="2819.003251953125" y="1098.8033740234375" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FLlcXo33fteFZTflUlvy-9" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;h1 class=&quot;c-article-satellite-title u-h1&quot; data-test=&quot;top-caption&quot; id=&quot;Fig7&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0.67em 0px 16px; font-weight: 700; -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; font-family: Harding, Palatino, serif; letter-spacing: min(max(-0.0117156rem, 4vw), -0.0390625rem); line-height: 1.4; box-sizing: inherit; word-break: break-word; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;Fig. 2&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="104" width="95" x="2701" y="460" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FLlcXo33fteFZTflUlvy-10" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;h3 class=&quot;c-article__sub-heading&quot; id=&quot;Sec5&quot; style=&quot;-webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, Roboto, Oxygen-Sans, Ubuntu, Cantarell, &amp;quot;Helvetica Neue&amp;quot;, sans-serif; letter-spacing: -0.0117156rem; font-size: 1.5rem; line-height: 1.24; box-sizing: inherit; font-style: normal; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); margin: 24px 0px 8px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;&quot;&gt;3. Immuno-editing through SCAAs and transcriptional regulation&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="74" width="753" x="2072" y="1895" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FLlcXo33fteFZTflUlvy-11" parent="1" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/png,;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="500" width="1055.27" x="404" y="2765" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FLlcXo33fteFZTflUlvy-12" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;a href=&quot;https://blog.crownbio.com/tumor-antigens-t-cell-therapy&quot;&gt;URL&lt;/a&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="60" x="298" y="2785" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FLlcXo33fteFZTflUlvy-13" parent="1" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/png,;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="338" width="338" x="2779.5" y="1966" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FLlcXo33fteFZTflUlvy-14" parent="1" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/png,;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="327" width="329.14" x="3166" y="1983" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FLlcXo33fteFZTflUlvy-15" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Epigenome reorganization preferentially silences neoantigen&lt;/b&gt;s, (that is, epigenetic immuno-editing, Fig. 2b,c)&lt;br&gt;We collated the chromatin accessibility of all genetic loci where a protein-changing mutation was detected.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;They found that: Neoantigens enriched in closed chromatin (SCAA loss), OR = 1.46 (P &amp;lt; 0.05), and this observation was also true on the individual cancer level&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Such loss are stronger in MMRd tumors than MMRp&lt;br&gt;→&amp;nbsp; Neoantigen loci are preferentially epigenetically silenced&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Transcriptional expression of neoantigens&lt;/b&gt;. (Fig. 2d)&lt;br&gt;Clonal neoantigens enriched in: Low / variable expression genes&lt;br&gt;Depleted in: Highly expressed genes&lt;br&gt;→ Neoantigens avoid highly visible genes&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Allele-specific expression of neoantigens&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Clonal neoantigens more likely not expressed, OR = 1.53&lt;br&gt;~50% neoantigens are transcriptionally silenced&lt;br&gt;→&amp;nbsp; Occurs across multiple tumor regions&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Clonal neoantigens are enriched in genes with low expression and/or in regions of closed chromatin and are further depleted through allele-specific expression modulation.&amp;nbsp; All these processes of postgenetic immuno-editing are likely to have an underlying somatic epigenetic mechanism.&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="689" width="725" x="2073.5" y="1990" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FLlcXo33fteFZTflUlvy-17" parent="1" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/png,;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="344" width="678.25" x="2793" y="2352" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FLlcXo33fteFZTflUlvy-18" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;h1 class=&quot;c-article-satellite-title u-h1&quot; data-test=&quot;top-caption&quot; id=&quot;Fig7&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0.67em 0px 16px; font-weight: 700; -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; font-family: Harding, Palatino, serif; letter-spacing: min(max(-0.0117156rem, 4vw), -0.0390625rem); line-height: 1.4; box-sizing: inherit; word-break: break-word; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;Fig. 2&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="104" width="95" x="2730" y="1942" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FLlcXo33fteFZTflUlvy-20" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;h3 class=&quot;c-article__sub-heading&quot; id=&quot;Sec6&quot; style=&quot;-webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; letter-spacing: -0.0117156rem; font-size: 1.5rem; line-height: 1.24; box-sizing: inherit; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); margin: 24px 0px 8px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;4. Immune exclusion and suppression across tumor regions&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="87" width="694.86" x="3542" y="32" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FLlcXo33fteFZTflUlvy-22" parent="1" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/webp,;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="422.09" width="1137" x="3518" y="2842.91" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FLlcXo33fteFZTflUlvy-23" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nature.com/articles/s41416-023-02361-4/figures/2&quot;&gt;Cold and hot tumors&lt;/a&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="123" x="3513" y="2804.91" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FLlcXo33fteFZTflUlvy-25" parent="1" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/webp,;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="306.93" width="702" x="2001" y="2873" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FLlcXo33fteFZTflUlvy-26" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial; float: none; display: inline !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Neoantigens play a pivotal role in cancer immunotherapy by activating tumor-specific T cells without triggering autoimmunity&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial; float: none; display: inline !important;&quot;&gt;. Unlike self-antigens, which may lead to off-target effects, neoantigens are uniquely derived from tumor mutations and are processed and presented on the cell surface by major histocompatibility complex (MHC) molecules, making them recognizable to the immune system. Accurate neoantigen identification is essential for the development of personalized cancer vaccines, adoptive T cell therapies, and immune checkpoint inhibitors, which have revolutionized cancer treatment in recent years.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial; float: none; display: inline !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial; float: none; display: inline !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mtoz-biolabs.com/neoantigen-identification-service.html&quot;&gt;URL&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="308" width="612" x="2745" y="2866" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FLlcXo33fteFZTflUlvy-27" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="FOXP3+ CTLA-4+ Tregs (Immune suppresion)" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="36" width="262" x="3745" y="3265" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FLlcXo33fteFZTflUlvy-28" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;How the structure and composition of the TME contributed to immune evasion?&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fig 3a&lt;/b&gt;: Reduced cytotoxic T cells (CD8+ CTLs) Lower CTLs in: superficial tumor (P = 3×10⁻⁵) &amp;amp; invasive margin (P = 3×10⁻³) compared to normal mucosa&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fig 3b,c&lt;/b&gt;: Spatial exclusion: CTLs are farther from tumor cells (P &amp;lt; 10⁻¹⁶), greatest distance in superficial tumor&lt;br&gt;→ T cells cannot effectively reach cancer cells&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fig 3d&lt;/b&gt;: Immune suppression (Tregs): FOXP3+ CTLA-4+ Tregs increased in tumors: superficial tumor (P = 0.012); invasive margin (P = 0.01); node (P = 6×10⁻³)&lt;br&gt;→ Promotes immunosuppressive environment&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="260" width="1094" x="3533" y="109" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FLlcXo33fteFZTflUlvy-30" parent="1" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/webp,;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="769.78" width="1093" x="3528" y="417.85" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FLlcXo33fteFZTflUlvy-31" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;h1 class=&quot;c-article-satellite-title u-h1&quot; data-test=&quot;top-caption&quot; id=&quot;Fig7&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0.67em 0px 16px; font-weight: 700; -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; font-family: Harding, Palatino, serif; letter-spacing: min(max(-0.0117156rem, 4vw), -0.0390625rem); line-height: 1.4; box-sizing: inherit; word-break: break-word; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;Fig. 3&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="104" width="95" x="3513" y="353" as="geometry" />
